  "description": "Resolves the Hubble tension through the environment-dependent Cepheid clock bias predicted by the Temporal Equivalence Principle, measured against the inner-potential stellar velocity dispersion sigma_*. The prespecified primary full-ladder projection yields H0 = 70.463 +/- 0.972 km/s/Mpc (2.80 sigma residual, structurally bounded by the shared zero point); the host-level reconstruction yields H0 = 67.83 +/- 1.56 km/s/Mpc (0.26 sigma from Planck).",
